{"author":{"uri":{"label":"https://itunes.apple.com/us/reviews/id717377903"}, "name":{"label":"Bob 85262"}, "label":""}, "updated":{"label":"2026-10-24T11:55:56-07:00"}, "im:rating":{"label":"1"}, "im:version":{"label":"2026.42"}, "id":{"label":"14706611996"}, "title":{"label":"Expedia is not good if your itinerary changes"}, "content":{"label":"I recently had to make a change (drop 3 of 4 rooms for the first night) to a hotel reservation and I was outside of the 24 hours notice the hotel policy for changes, but Expedia has a longer notification period with the hotel, so they would not allow me to make the change.  However, upon checking in the Hotel front desk saw that I did call them in advance of the 24 hour hour no change period, so they compromised and only charged me for 2 rooms instead of 4.  A day later Expedia came back and charged me for the entire 4 rooms and explained that was THEIR policy.  I actually had to go back to the hotel and they again gave me the credit for the 2 unused rooms.  So in the end the hotel was very accommodating but Expedia got in the way and tried to make it worse.  Don’t recommend using Expedia unless you have to.  The small savings is not worth the hassle or risk.", "attributes":{"type":"text"}}, "link":{"attributes":{"rel":"related", "href":"https://itunes.apple.com/us/review?id=427916203&type=Purple%20Software"}}, "im:voteSum":{"label":"0"}, "im:contentType":{"attributes":{"term":"Application", "label":"Application"}}, "im:voteCount":{"label":"0"}}, 
{"author":{"uri":{"label":"https://itunes.apple.com/us/reviews/id1291473673"}, "name":{"label":"Louivis"}, "label":""}, "updated":{"label":"2026-10-24T10:55:40-07:00"}, "im:rating":{"label":"1"}, "im:version":{"label":"2026.42"}, "id":{"label":"14706415699"}, "title":{"label":"Watch your booking with Expedia"}, "content":{"label":"I booked a $2,448.84 stay at The Strand in Turks and Caicos for October 26–29 and paid nearly $200 for travel insurance. Due to severe weather forecasts, we contacted Expedia to cancel or postpone the trip, but they said they could not reach the hotel.\n\nWe were told the reservation was only 50% refundable, while the rest depended on a separate insurance claim that could take 10–15 days, with no guarantee of approval. Despite paying for insurance, Expedia provided no timely solution, clear guidance, or assurance that our money would be protected.\n\nWhat was meant to be a relaxing birthday celebration became a stressful experience. I am deeply disappointed with Expedia’s communication and customer service and will think twice before booking with them again.", "attributes":{"type":"text"}}, "link":{"attributes":{"rel":"related", "href":"https://itunes.apple.com/us/review?id=427916203&type=Purple%20Software"}}, "im:voteSum":{"label":"0"}, "im:contentType":{"attributes":{"term":"Application", "label":"Application"}}, "im:voteCount":{"label":"0"}}, 
